    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "CATHAY\nPACIFIC\nAIRWAYS\nTIME \u0026 FARE SCHEDULES\nEFFECTIVE: 22nd October, 1967.\nFor Schedule 1st - 21st October see insert\nMEMBER OF THE SWIRE GROUP",
      "CATHAY PACIFIC AIRWAYS\nHONG KONG\nBANGKOK\nCALCUTTA\nFUKUOKA\nJESSELTON\nKUALA LUMPUR\nMANILA\nNAGOYA\nOKINAWA\nOSAKA/KYOTO\nPHNOM PENH\nSAIGON\nSEOUL\nSINGAPORE\nTAIPEI\nTOKYO\nVIENTIANE\nSEOUL\nTOKYO\nN'AGOYA\nKYOTO\nOSAKA\nFUKUOKA\nOKINAWA\nTAIPEI\nHONG KONG\nCALCUTTA\nVIENTIANE\nMANILA\nBANGKOK\nPHNOM\nPENH\nSAIGON\nMELTON\nKUALA LUMPUR\nSINGAPORE\nRIMSON TRAVEL SERVICE, INC\n5 BOYLSTON STREET, HARVARD SQ\nCAMBRIDGE, MASS. 02138\nTEL. UN 8-2600",
      "International\nbusiness?\nDon't waste time.\nJet there with Cathay Pacific. Serves more\ninternational business centres of the Orient\nthan any other airline. With a hard headed\nschedule\nthat means\nbusiness.\nJapan. From Oct 1,\n3 jets everyday\nfrom Hong Kong.\n21 jets every week.\nServing Tokyo, Osaka,\nNagoya and Fukuoka.\n17 jets every week\nbetween Taipei and\nJapan.\nSeoul. Fast developing\ncapital ot a tough nation.\nPotential recognized ...\nCathay Pacific has daily\njets to Seoul from Hong\nKong, 4 jets from Tokyo\nevery week and 2 from\nOsaka.\n-\nOthers. Daily jets between Bangkok and Hong\nKong. 9 jets every week between Manila and\nHong Kong. Daily\njets between\nSingapore and\nHong Kong. An\nHong Kong. What more would you expect from\nHong Kong's international airline? More jets\nthrough Hong Kong than any other! We've 88\nevery week... nearly twice as many as No. 2.\nunprecedented\n183 flights every\nweek between the\n17 major cities of\nthe Orient.\nBusiness is business. And ours is air travel-international air travel.\nCATHAY PACIFIC\nTHE AIRLINE THAT KNOWS THE ORIENT BEST\nHONG KONG • BANGKOK CALCUTTA . FUKUOKA • JESSELTON • KUALA LUMPUR • MANILA• NAGOYA OKINAWA • OSAKA/KYOTO• PHNOM PENH • SAIGON • SEOUL • SINGAPORE • TAIPEI • TOKYO• VIENTIANE"
    ],
